# Live LLM endpoint for `pnpm test:live` — copy this file to `.env` and fill
# it in. `.env` is gitignored; nothing in it is ever committed, so each
# developer points at whatever they actually run.
#
# Any OpenAI-compatible chat endpoint works:
#   LM Studio   http://localhost:1234/v1
#   Ollama      http://localhost:11434/v1
#   llama.cpp   http://localhost:8080/v1
#   a hosted provider, with STORYENGINE_LIVE_API_KEY set
#
# When these are unset (no .env, fresh clone, CI) the live suite skips and
# everything stays green — the variables are the switch, not just the address.

# Base URL of the endpoint, including the /v1 segment.
STORYENGINE_LIVE_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1

# A model id the endpoint can serve. `curl $STORYENGINE_LIVE_BASE_URL/models`
# lists what yours offers.
STORYENGINE_LIVE_MODEL=

# Only if the endpoint requires one. Local servers usually want none.
# STORYENGINE_LIVE_API_KEY=

# Optional: a model on the same endpoint that sees pictures (Ollama's llava,
# LM Studio's qwen2-vl, a hosted vision model). Set it and the live suite also
# sends one picture and checks the endpoint takes it — 25 E15.
# STORYENGINE_LIVE_VISION_MODEL=
